course: dictionary
lesson: 4497
title: Words that haunt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The words around it show which meaning the writer wants. «The old house is haunted by a ghost» is about a spooky place in a story. But «The memory of that day still haunts him» is not about ghosts at all: the memory keeps coming back to his mind and upsets him.
explain: Look at the words near haunt. In «warm, insect-haunted ponds», the word is joined to insect, so the ponds are places where lots of insects are often found. Always test your meaning: put it into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: Haunt can also be a noun, meaning a place you visit often. «The café is my favourite haunt» means the café is somewhere you love going again and again. To tell which job haunt is doing, ask: is it a place, or is something doing the haunting?
fact: Haunt can be a verb: ghosts haunt places, and worries can haunt you.
fact: «Haunt» as a verb means to keep appearing in a place, or to keep coming back to your mind.
fact: A «favourite haunt» is a place you go to very often.
fact: «Come back to haunt you» means a past mistake causes trouble later on.
fact: There is no evidence that ghosts exist; haunted-house tales are told for fun and for spooky stories.
exercise: «The old house is haunted by a ghost.» What does haunted mean here? | Very cold in winter | Painted bright yellow | *Visited by a ghost that keeps appearing | A scary film about a house
exercise: «The café is her favourite haunt.» What is a haunt here? | *A place she visits often | A scary film | A ghost
exercise: «The memory of that day still haunts him.» What does haunts mean? | He forgets it quickly | He is going to a party | *He keeps thinking about it and it upsets him | He dances all night
test: Which sentence uses haunt as a place, not a verb? | «Worries haunt my sleep.» | «The ghost will haunt the attic.» | *«The café is my favourite haunt.»
test: What does «come back to haunt you» mean? | A happy surprise | *A mistake that causes trouble later | A ghost that returns home
exam: In «warm, insect-haunted ponds», what does haunted suggest? | *Ponds where lots of insects are often found | Ponds that are very deep and cold | Ponds that are scary and full of ghosts | Ponds that have been painted blue
